The general idea behind this app is one where I arrive at the home page and it presents me with a magic link login, using classic 
click this link sends an email through resend and once the user clicks on the link redirects to the logged in gated app.

For the magic link, consider what the cool kids use, ideally what Kent C Dodds does on his older React courses, unless there is a better way.

Now for the app, it presents the user with a free type edit box similar to the chatgpt or claude chat window, but inside the edit box it should only allow pre defined words and using a typeahead concept, where the actual words are in black, and the predicted next word is in greyed out text. I want you to use your judgement here as to the implementation of this, as I have also in the past used react select but then it presents choices as a dropdown. The choices would come from a pre approved bucket of words.

I want to run a grill-me session on the best way to manage these is it in a flatfile or yml file, or a more structured table in a mysql database, I want to experiment with a mysql in railway setup. The idea behind this would be to have a constrained way to build a prompt for later translation requests.

Some example prompts which add to the already baked in system prompt could be:

You are a Dutch teacher help me to write an email to my college profressor.
You are a French businessman and give me advice to write an informal letter to the business adminstration
You are a german friend helping me to write a speech in german for my friends birthday party
You are an italian real estate agent help me to write a motivation letter to buy the house in Italian

So there are some examples, see if you can find a logical compartmentalisation, I dont really want the user to have full free typing reign, but I also want some flexibility in the wording, but placeholders would help, so definitely a list of all languages, and as soon as user type you are a Du (it would fill in Dutch, or Ger, German etc, or just to select from a long list, like in google translate. Again grill-me on wether TLLM from Google would work or a standard Open AI api call or Anthropic call or a combination, or would Jev Typesafe work???

So then when system prompt done, the next tab or enter key should position cursor in the actual language translation box, the user types their email, letter text whatever

So example would be: Dear Mr Jones, thank you for the time today on the phone. I would be interested in the work schedule you proopose so on and so forth.

then tab out to a translate button and the text would be sent as LLM api call with system prompt and return the result which is displayed to user. A handy copy link or icon which copies the translated text.

